{
  "scope": "All examples use the same g(x)=x signed H walk from a localized (0,R) on C_(4M), without an address-dependent staircase or added sheet measurement. Coefficients are the normalized effective counting and fixed character responses of the specified preparation. Repeat terminal launches for different calibration settings. Prediction across a DO herald requires fixed shared components through that flight and the coherent direction-only instrument.",
  "one_left_formula": "Let D_j=sum b_k cos(4*pi*k*j/M). W_n=2^(n+1)P_{n+1}(n-1,R) =n+2*sum_{j=1}^{n-1}(n-j)D_j. The symmetric second difference is 2D_n. Adjacent LR/RL exchanges raise area by two, and every witness word is positive.",
  "six_tick_count": "The (1,R) numerator at t=5 is 4+2c-4D_1+2D_2-4D_3+2D_4. The one-left record through six ticks supplies all four lags. Subtract to recover c. At this same port pure count gives 6/32, unforced k=0 gives zero, while uniform signed characters give 4/32 when the five even-area residues are distinct. Nyquist is inseparable from k=0 for even M.",
  "identified_class": "For H=M/gcd(M,2), identify s=fold_H((2/gcd(M,2))*k) in the inverse real Fourier transform. For even M, conjugation and adding M/2 have identical base-port laws: area at each depth has parity n*x0+n(n-1)/2, independent of history. The common sign survives native repeated coordinate/DO readouts at known ticks on one localized parity; coherent inter-parity preparations and operations need not share this alias. For a class s the physical phase distance from the nearest multiple of pi is pi*s/H.",
